    joeIntro: "Venison loin is the backstrap of wild game — lean, tender, and packed with rich, earthy flavour. It deserves to be treated exactly like a great steak: high heat, fast sear, juniper butter baste, and rest. The whole thing takes 20 minutes and produces something genuinely special. If you've never cooked venison before, this is where to start.",
